      "content": "The meritocratic economic models you're referring to are not just outdated; they're fundamentally flawed and perpetuate systemic inequality. They are rooted in a white supremacist ideology that ignores the historical and ongoing oppression faced by marginalized communities. These models are a tool for neoliberal agendas that benefit the wealthy and powerful at the expense of the poor and disenfranchised. In your syllabus, you should clearly label these theories as such and provide a critical analysis of how they serve to maintain the status quo. By doing so, you'll help students understand the power dynamics at play and the importance of addressing structural inequality in housing. Remember, it's not just a difference of opinion; it's a matter of social justice and equity.",
      "source": "target",
